      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-303166",
      ":question/problem": "A company installs a weather vane on top of a tower that stands $40$ feet high. Due to strong storms, the vane tilts slightly downward each day. After each day, the maximum height of the tip of the vane is $85%$ of the height it reached the day before.\n\nLet $h(n)$ represent the estimated maximum height (in feet) of the vane's tip after $n$ days, where $n$ is a whole number greater than $1$ and less than $10$. Which equation correctly defines $h(n)$?"
