      ":question/problem": "A lighthouse installs a beacon on top of a tower that stands $50$ feet high. Due to salty sea winds, the beacon\u2019s maximum height decreases slightly each day. After each day, the maximum height of the tip of the beacon is $70%$ of the height it reached the day before.\n\nLet $h(n)$ represent the estimated maximum height (in feet) of the beacon's tip after $n$ days, where $n$ is a whole number greater than $1$ and less than $10$. Which equation correctly defines $h(n)$?"
